WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.760
Exactly a year ago at San
Francisco we introduced a new

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:11.192
division in Microsoft called
Microsoft AI Research.

00:00:11.192 --> 00:00:14.630
We actually have the mission
to democratize AI for everyone.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:19.780
It has been a very
exciting year in 2017.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.630
We expected and delivered.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.360
A very exciting year.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.940
So I'm here to share some
of the progress with you.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.510
I appreciate this
opportunity to show you,

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:34.040
especially, some
very practical ways

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:38.120
that AI is helping everyone
to improve our lives.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.780
So everyone is talking
about AI nowadays.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.654
But AI is really not new.

00:00:44.654 --> 00:00:48.927
AI was really something, really
the ultimate goal that for

00:00:48.927 --> 00:00:52.175
brilliant minds,
people like Alan Turing,

00:00:52.175 --> 00:00:55.936
those people imagined that
some day, if we have this

00:00:55.936 --> 00:01:00.380
unbelievable computing power,
what could we really do.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:05.030
The first thing that Alan Turing
really imagined was doing AI

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:08.130
is really mimicking
human intelligence.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:12.610
And at Microsoft, our very own
Bill Gates, when he created

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:17.010
the Microsoft Research 26 years
ago, he imagined that someday,

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:22.260
computers could see, hear, talk,
and understand the human beings.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:23.960
That's really generalized AI.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:29.430
And the AI is now happening
fast, why is that?

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:32.290
To me it's really three forces
that are converging to make

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:33.850
these things happen.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:37.246
It's really the big data, more
and more aware with the web,

00:01:37.246 --> 00:01:39.330
with IoT and everything.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:42.459
And massive computing power,
especially with the cloud.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:46.860
But most recently especially
with breakthrough algorithms

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.850
like deep learning or deep
neural nets that really moved

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:52.620
the AI from the labs
to the mainstream.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:58.890
So today we are going to talk
to you about every day AI.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:04.670
It's really the AI is available
to everyone, everywhere,

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:08.770
and then whatever you do in your
personal and professional life.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:10.260
So how AI's going to help.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:16.180
But in many ways,
if you just read articles in

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:20.580
the general press, AI probably
has gotten a bad reputation,

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:25.400
because much of the AI
discussions about humans versus

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:31.130
machines but
not enough about AI potentials.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:34.711
We know AI will transform
every business and

00:02:34.711 --> 00:02:38.776
help every life to potentially
solve some of those

00:02:38.776 --> 00:02:41.990
societal challenges
that we all face.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.260
You might ask that,
that all sounds great, but

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.060
what about Microsoft AI,
what's so

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.660
unique about what we do
at Microsoft about AI?

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:59.660
Well we believe that AI comes
down to one thing, people.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:05.000
AI will amplify human ingenuity,
making people the heroes.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.890
And then driving a healthy
connection between humans and

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:08.790
the machines.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.420
That's what we
believe at Microsoft.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:15.150
After all, that's really
about the Microsoft mission.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:17.160
That is,
empower every person and

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:21.180
every organization on
the planet to achieve more.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.090
Now I will even add, with AI.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.330
It's really a powerful mission.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.130
And not too long ago, our CEO,

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:32.470
Satya Nadella shared
our world view.

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:34.951
That is the intelligent
cloud and

00:03:34.951 --> 00:03:37.703
the intelligent
edge infused by AI.

00:03:37.703 --> 00:03:41.557
In a way, it's really about
ubiquitous computing and

00:03:41.557 --> 00:03:46.334
ambient intelligence finally
happening, with PCs, phones, and

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:49.190
then more and more IOT devices.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:51.480
Just imagine that you
walk into any room, you

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:57.490
know you walk to a speaker, you
walk to a screen, or you don't

00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:01.270
even realize that those things
happening, existing in the room.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:02.560
Then you can already, you know,

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.150
talk to Cortana,
to get things done.

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:08.931
Maybe across the room with the
help of far field cameras and

00:04:08.931 --> 00:04:11.050
far field speakers.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:15.914
So our goal is really to help
everyone, everywhere and

00:04:15.914 --> 00:04:18.780
take advantage of AI every day.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:22.133
So that's exactly why Satya and
I actually created it,

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:24.640
our AI in the research division.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:26.220
And a little over a year ago.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.155
It has been a really
exciting year.

00:04:28.155 --> 00:04:31.771
And with more than 8,000
researchers and engineers

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:36.510
